% Under -v a session's queries are counted like any others, numbered after
% the program's own; .plan counts the query it ran, and a line that was
% rejected still takes its number.  -vv notes a mixed-type comparison once
% for the rule, however many queries read it.
v(1).
v(a).
small(X) :- v(X), X < 5.

v(X)?
small(X)?
